{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1025335-enlightenment-and-paradox-q","id":1025335,"title":"Enlightenment and Paradox (Q)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-02T01:18:30-08:00","id":1025335,"title":"Enlightenment and Paradox (Q)","content":"If I'm reading the Paradox section right:<br /> - A mage can release Paradox, possible tainting the spell or their surroundings. If it does, the taint/Condition lasts _shorter_ if the mage is more enlightened.<br /> - A mage can also internalize Paradox, possibly taking damage or gaining a Condition. If it does, this effect lasts _longer_ if the mage is more enlightened.<br /> <br /> My question is: why? I get the ooc factor - we like having Conditions, 'cause they're interesting and yield Beats. But what's the ic explanation? Why does being _more_ enlightened make the effect of internalized Paradox _worse_? I'm trying to figure out how the setting works internally, and am having trouble placing this.<br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Freelance Author and Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1713-mistress-of-whispers","name":"mistress of whispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1713_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T01:59:07-08:00","id":1025342,"title":"","content":"Imagine you have ten gallons of water. You add one gallon of wine. No matter how much water or wine you add to this mixture, it'll never be pure again.<br /> <br /> Imagine you have ten gallons of liquid composed of five gallons of water and five gallons of wine. You add one gallon of wine. To restore the mixture to its previous balance, all you need to do is add a gallon of water.<br /> <br /> Paradox and enlightenment work the same way. If your enlightenment is only middling, adding a little bit of paradox is not going to create a big change in what you are. If your enlightenment is very high, adding the same amount of paradox is going to create a much bigger change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12787-logos","name":"logos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T02:04:59-08:00","id":1025344,"title":"","content":"Very eloquently put I was not sure how to answer this and now your analogy paints a picture that I can follow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T02:31:52-08:00","id":1025347,"title":"","content":"Ha, thanks, that makes it a lot clearer <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Freelance Author and Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1713-mistress-of-whispers","name":"mistress of whispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1713_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T08:08:11-08:00","id":1025442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mistress of whispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1025335-enlightenment-and-paradox-q#post1025335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why does being _more_ enlightened make the effect of internalized Paradox _worse_? I'm trying to figure out how the setting works internally, and am having trouble placing this.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the Condition lapses naturally the Abyss taints your Nimbus and makes all your spells risk Paradox until you can scour it out. Having a greater concern for/awareness of your magic's impact on the world gives you more time to discharge the Condition without affecting your magic in the long term \u2014 the Condition itself is not <i>actually worse</i> just because its <i>maximum duration</i> is longer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T15:01:43-08:00","id":1025582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1025335-enlightenment-and-paradox-q?p=1025442#post1025442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Condition lapses naturally the Abyss taints your Nimbus and makes all your spells risk Paradox until you can scour it out. Having a greater concern for/awareness of your magic's impact on the world gives you more time to discharge the Condition without affecting your magic in the long term \u2014 the Condition itself is not <i>actually worse</i> just because its <i>maximum duration</i> is longer.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Precisely. The Condition lasting longer is a good thing, because it gives you <i>a larger safe window</i> to fix it before you need to start scouring your pattern.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T15:48:29-08:00","id":1025599,"title":"","content":"Seconding Satchel here; Abyssal Conditions can be resolved generally by the character acting in a manner that symbolically lets them overcome the Abyss. They prove they're mightier than it, they successfully contain it, etc. The Wise can not merely resist the Abyss but fight it. The unWise allow its chaotic power into their souls far more easily, causing it to wreak havoc on their lives and those around them, to the point where the only way to get rid of it is to sacrifice a piece of yourself to the Abyss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T17:57:03-08:00","id":1025649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1025335-enlightenment-and-paradox-q?p=1025582#post1025582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Precisely. The Condition lasting longer is a good thing, because it gives you <i>a larger safe window</i> to fix it before you need to start scouring your pattern.</div> </div> </div> </div>And by the opposite metric, one of the many things that makes Scelesti horrifying in this edition is how fast they can become a problem magically, between Falling Wisdom making Paradox Conditions into a viable recurrent source of Arcane Beats and tainting your magic providing more free Reach at higher Gnosis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T21:35:27-08:00","id":1025717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mistress of whispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1025335-enlightenment-and-paradox-q#post1025335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why does being _more_ enlightened make the effect of internalized Paradox _worse_? I'm trying to figure out how the setting works internally, and am having trouble placing this.<br /> <br /> Thanks!</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't. That's what it looks like on first read (and was how I thought it works when I first read it), but when the Condition ends it doesn't just go away (unlike with non-Paradox-derived Conditions), it stops manifesting itself as a Condition and instead integrates itself into your pattern and forces an extra Paradox die onto <i>every</i> casting you make until you Scour your pattern. In effect, once that duration runs out, things get worse, so the duration being longer is actually a good thing. While you <i>do</i> still have the Condition, there are other ways to get rid of it <i>without</i> letting it integrate itself into your Pattern (such as successfully casting a spell that has a Paradox pool of 0 when you have the Abyssal Imago Condition, or completely containing a Paradox while you have the Abyssal Backlash Condition). If you pull that off while the Condition is active, the Condition resolves properly and the Abyssal influence is gone rather than integrating into your Pattern. Having higher Wisdom gives you a longer timespan during which to successfully do this. An Enlightened-Wisdom Mage has an entire story's worth of time to successfully entirely contain a Paradox when they have the Abyssal Backlash Condition in order to get rid of it without having to Scour. A Falling-Wisdom Mage has to do it in the next Scene, otherwise it'll integrate itself and the only way to get rid of it will be to Scour (and you'll be rolling Paradox on every single spell you cast until you do).<br /> <br /> It looks backwards until you read the elaborating text that explains what happens when the Condition lapses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T00:07:10-08:00","id":1025763,"title":"","content":"Paradox-Wisdom relationship is cool in the way that being High Wisdom has it's merits when it comes to paradox management, and Low Wisdom has it's merits too; it's just that you need to play around it if you want to make it beneficial. Very different experiences, both viable, and both wouldn't feel so proper without mechanical structure. One of the cases where simple mechanics worldbuild more than kilometers of lore dumps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T02:57:12-08:00","id":1025799,"title":"","content":"Thanks for explaining the difference between _resolving_ the Condition vs letting it lapse. That's indeed good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Freelance Author and Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1713-mistress-of-whispers","name":"mistress of whispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1713_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T20:51:19-07:00","id":1086448,"title":"","content":"Hi! Sorry for necro-raising this thread, but I have a related question about the resolution terms of Paradox Conditions.<br /> <br /> The book says that Paradox Conditions, unlike normal Conditions, have two resolution mechanics: 1) to actively accept the negative consequence of the Paradox, and 2) to allow the Paradox to lapse. Yet when describing each particular condition, there are three different resolution options: accept the negative effect, purge the spell from the mage's pattern, and letting the condition to lapse. The first option excludes the latter two, while the second option says &quot;scour the condition&quot; instead of &quot;scour the taint from the mage's pattern, which is somewhat confusing.<br /> <br /> a) Can you Scour a Paradox Condition before it lapses?<br /> <br /> b) Does lapsing + scouring effectively net you 2 arcane beats, instead of just one through the first resolution option?<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T21:05:48-07:00","id":1086454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zooroos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1025335-enlightenment-and-paradox-q?p=1086448#post1086448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi! Sorry for necro-raising this thread, but I have a related question about the resolution terms of Paradox Conditions.<br /> <br /> The book says that Paradox Conditions, unlike normal Conditions, have two resolution mechanics: 1) to actively accept the negative consequence of the Paradox, and 2) to allow the Paradox to lapse. Yet when describing each particular condition, there are three different resolution options: accept the negative effect, purge the spell from the mage's pattern, and letting the condition to lapse. The first option excludes the latter two, while the second option says &quot;scour the condition&quot; instead of &quot;scour the taint from the mage's pattern, which is somewhat confusing.<br /> <br /> a) Can you Scour a Paradox Condition before it lapses?<br /> <br /> b) Does lapsing + scouring effectively net you 2 arcane beats, instead of just one through the first resolution option?<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance!</div> </div> </div> </div>No and no. Scouring the Condition before lapsing would defeat the point of there being a Duration chart for them and that in turn means &quot;double-dipping&quot; would be the default outcome of that resolution method.<br /> <br /> The tidiest way to represent this might be to have the Duration be the point at which the individualized Condition effect coalesces into the generalized taint and have the Arcane Beat granted upon scouring it after that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}